The operational audit has exposed a concrete bridge defect: for `[True, None, None, False]`, the candidate’s public `sortThirdResult` definition reduces to the unchanged input, while the frozen source algorithm returns `[False, None, None, True]`. I’m also compiling the supplied K semantics fresh for a string witness, because `sort.k` explicitly implements lexicographic string sorting while the generated Lean `SortVal`/`SortIterable` types omit the K `Str` constructor—an independent Stage 4 domain-weakening concern.
